<title>SWEDEN: Swedbank issues $150 mln undated loan.</title>
<headline>Swedbank issues $150 mln undated loan.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish investment bank Swedbank said on Monday it had issued $150 million in undated subordinated debt.  </p>
<p>Swedbank said in a statement it had the option to redeem the loan after ten years with the approval of the Swedish Financial Supervisory Authority.</p>
<p>It said the issue was part of the restructuring of the bank's Swedish group's subordinated loan capital to longer maturities and a larger share of undated subordinated debt.</p>
<p>-- Abigail Schmelz, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1003</p>
